center;\n    border-top: 1px solid #e2e2e2;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2;\n    margin-top: 34px;\n    padding: 14px 0;\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- Sidebar ---------- */\n  .sidebar h2 {\n    font-weight: 400;\n    font-size: 21px;\n    margin: 8px 0 10px;\n    padding-bottom: 12px;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2;\n    color: #123c28;\n  }\n  .sidebar ul {\n    margin: 0 0 6px;\n    padding-left: 22px;\n  }\n  .sidebar li { margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  .sidebar ul ul { padding-left: 22px; margin-top: 4px; }\n  .sidebar ul ul { list-style-type: circle; }\n  .sidebar ul ul ul { list-style-type: square; }\n\n  .donate-block {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 16px;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n    margin-bottom: 26px;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    background: #fdf0f5;\n    border: 1px dashed #d98cae;\n    color: #a1436e;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 2px;\n  }\n  .heart-placeholder { width: 62px; height: 55px; flex: 0 0 62px; }\n  .donate-text { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #20aa76; }\n\n  .help-item { margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  .help-item p { margin: 2px 0 14px; }\n  .help-sep { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e2e2e2; margin: 14px 0; }\n\n  /* ---------- Floating widgets ---------- */\n  .float-widget {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 24px;\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    padding: 7px 12px;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    color: #0c3c26;\n    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\n  }\n  .w-getting-help { top: 848px; color: #20aa76; }\n  .w-language { top: 897px; right: 46px; font-weight: 400; }\n  .w-version { top: 944px; right: 84px; font-weight: 400; }\n  .to-top {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 24px;\n    top: 992px;\n    width: 40px;\n    height: 32px;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    background: #fff;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    color: #20aa76;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"topbar\">\n  <div class=\"logo\">django</div>\n  <nav class=\"mainnav\">\n    <a href=\"#\">Overview</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">Download</a>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"active\">Documentation</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">News</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">Code</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">Issues</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">Community</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">Foundation</a>\n    <a href=\"#\">&#9829; Donate</a>\n  </nav>\n  <div class=\"searchbox\">\n    <span>Search (&#8984; K)</span>\n    <span class=\"icon\">&#128269;</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"theme-toggle\">&#9686;</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"doc-banner\">\n  <h1>Documentation</h1>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"survey\">\n  <h2>Django Developer Survey</h2>\n  <p>The Django Software Foundation is once again partnering with JetBrains to run the 2026 Django Developer Survey 📊 Help us better understand how Django is being used around the world and guide future technical and community decisions. <strong>Read more on the Django blog</strong>.</p>\n  <p>Please help us spread the word by sharing the survey with your communities and on social media 📣 The more diverse the responses, the better the results for everyone.</p>\n  <a class=\"survey-btn\" href=\"#\">Take the survey ✨</a>\n</section>\n\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <main class=\"content\">\n    <h1>Django 4.1.12 release notes <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#\">&para;</a></h1>\n\n    <p class=\"date\">October 4, 2023</p>\n\n    <p>Django 4.1.12 fixes a security issue with severity &ldquo;moderate&rdquo; in 4.1.11.</p>\n\n    <h2>CVE-2023-43665: Denial-of-service possibility in <code>django.utils.text.Truncator</code> <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#\">&para;</a></h2>\n\n    <p>Following the fix for <a class=\"literal-link\" href=\"#\"><code>CVE 2019-14232</code></a>, the regular expressions used in the implementation of <code>django.utils.text.Truncator</code>&rsquo;s <code>chars()</code> and <code>words()</code> methods (with <code>html=True</code>) were revised and improved. However, these regular expressions still exhibited linear backtracking complexity, so when given a very long, potentially malformed HTML input, the evaluation would still be slow, leading to a potential denial of service vulnerability.</p>\n\n    <p>The <code>chars()</code> and <code>words()</code> methods are used to implement the <a class=\"literal-link\" href=\"#\"><code>truncatechars_html</code></a> and <a class=\"literal-link\" href=\"#\"><code>truncatewords_html</code></a> template filters, which were thus also vulnerable.</p>\n\n    <p>The input processed by <code>Truncator</code>, when operating in HTML mode, has been limited to the first five million characters in order to avoid potential performance and memory issues.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"prevnext\">\n      <a href=\"#\">&#8249;&nbsp; Django 4.1.13 release notes</a>\n      <a href=\"#\">Django 4.1.11 release notes &nbsp;&#8250;</a>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  <aside class=\"sidebar\">\n    <h2>Support Django!</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"donate-block\">\n      <figure class=\"placeholder heart-placeholder\">[Image: pixel heart]</figure>\n      <div class=\"donate-text\">Agence Debord donated to the Django Software Foundation to support Django development. Donate today!</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2>Contents</h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">Django 4.1.12 release notes</a>\n        <ul>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">CVE-2023-43665: Denial-of-service possibility in <code>django.utils.text.Truncator</code></a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2>Browse</h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Prev: <a href=\"#\">Django 4.1.13 release notes</a></li>\n      <li>Next: <a href=\"#\">Django 4.1.11 release notes</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">Table of contents</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">General Index</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">Python Module Index</a></li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2>You are here:</h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">Django 5.2 documentation</a>\n        <ul>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Release notes</a>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Django 4.1.12 release notes</li>\n            </ul>\n          </li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2>Getting help</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"help-item\">\n      <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n      <p>Try the FAQ &mdash; it's got answers to many common questions.</p>\n    </div>\n    <hr class=\"help-sep\">\n\n    <div class=\"help-item\">\n      <a href=\"#\">Index</a>, <a href=\"#\">Module Index</a>, or <a href=\"#\">Table of Contents</a>\n      <p>Handy when looking for specific information.</p>\n    </div>\n    <hr class=\"help-sep\">\n\n    <div class=\"help-item\">\n      <a href=\"#\">Django Discord Server</a>\n      <p>Join the Django Discord Community.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"float-widget w-getting-help\">Getting Help</div>\n    <div class=\"float-widget w-language\">Language: <strong>en</strong></div>\n    <div class=\"float-widget w-version\">Documentation version: <strong>5.2</strong></div>\n    <div class=\"to-top\">&#9650;</div>\n  </aside>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>"
